"<strong>Setups in the demo:</strong> Simple random: pocket change; Stratified: {#} from each section; Cluster: two blocks of seats; Systematic: every 20th seat; Convenience: the ones by the door; Self selected: who chooses the videos?; Randomized: a coin decides; Means of skewed reaction times, n = {#}; Pocket change: sums of n = {#}; Uniform seconds: n = {#} makes a triangle; Bimodal commutes: n = {#}; n = {#}: the means are the population.",
"The picture is a lecture hall of {#} students, {#} rows of {#} seats, with the board at the front and the door at the back left. Each seat’s color is that student’s value; the legend under the hall gives the values (in Day light is few cents and dark many, in Night the other way round). The four sections of four rows, A to D, are the strata.",
"<strong>Sampling methods</strong> (the first view): the <strong>Sampling method</strong> switch picks Simple random, Stratified, Cluster, Systematic or Convenience. <strong>Draw a sample</strong> takes one sample of {#} and rings the students picked; <strong>Draw {#}</strong> takes {#} at once; <strong>Play</strong> draws them one at a time, then faster, up to the next {#}. Each sample’s mean x̄ drops as a dot into its method’s row in the lower graph; the green line is the population mean μ.",
"The Readouts give <strong>Samples drawn</strong>, <strong>This sample’s mean x̄</strong>, <strong>Population mean μ</strong>, <strong>Mean of the x̄’s</strong>, <strong>Bias, mean of x̄’s − μ</strong> and <strong>Spread, s of the x̄’s</strong> for the method chosen. <strong>Reset</strong> clears every method’s samples.",
