"<strong>B. {#} samples by each method.</strong> Press <strong>Reset</strong> (in the strip above the hall) so every method starts from zero. With <strong>Simple random</strong> chosen, press <strong>Draw {#}</strong>. Then choose Stratified and press Draw {#}; then Cluster, Systematic and Convenience, Draw {#} each. Each method now has exactly {#} samples (<strong>Samples drawn</strong> in the Readouts). Look at the five rows of dots in the lower graph. Press <strong>Record reading</strong> once: it records one row for each method. Press <strong>Export to worksheet</strong> (Table {#}), then <strong>Clear</strong>.",
